            "results_error_message": "Something went wrong. Please try again.",
            "type_1_name": "The Muse",
            "type_1_tagline": "You don’t just want attention. You want to feel unmistakably desired.",
            "type_1_percent": 8,
            "type_1_dim1_label": "Dominance",
            "type_1_dim1_value": 40,
            "type_1_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_1_dim2_value": 60,
            "type_1_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_1_dim3_value": 38,
            "type_1_locked_text": "A lingering look, a softer voice, or attention that keeps returning to you can affect you more than anything obvious. Your desire grows when you feel someone noticing every small reaction—and when their interest feels focused, personal, and impossible to mistake.\n\nYou don’t simply want to be admired; you want to feel your presence changing the energy between you. Bottom line: you’re most turned on when attention becomes undeniable desire.",
            "type_1_customer_tags": "quiz-type-1",
            "type_2_name": "The Dreamer",
            "type_2_tagline": "Reality rarely turns you on as much as what your mind can turn it into.",
            "type_2_percent": 14,
            "type_2_dim1_label": "Dominance",
            "type_2_dim1_value": 36,
            "type_2_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_2_dim2_value": 55,
            "type_2_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_2_dim3_value": 76,
            "type_2_locked_text": "Your desire often begins before anything actually happens. A voice, a fictional scenario, or one perfectly chosen detail can open an entire world in your mind, allowing anticipation and imagination to make the moment feel more intense.\n\nYou need more than attraction—you need a scene immersive enough to step outside ordinary life and become another version of yourself. Bottom line: imagination isn’t an accessory to your pleasure; it’s where your pleasure begins.",
            "type_2_customer_tags": "quiz-type-2",
            "type_3_name": "The Switch",
            "type_3_tagline": "Your real turn-on isn’t control or surrender. It’s the moment one becomes the other.",
            "type_3_percent": 21,
            "type_3_dim1_label": "Dominance",
            "type_3_dim1_value": 68,
            "type_3_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_3_dim2_value": 88,
            "type_3_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_3_dim3_value": 82,
            "type_3_locked_text": "Sometimes you want to set the pace, provoke a reaction, and feel someone respond to your confidence. At other times, you’re drawn to someone compelling enough to make you willingly release control and follow their lead.\n\nTrust, chemistry, and mood decide which side of you appears—but the unexpected shift is often what excites you most. Bottom line: you’re turned on by the freedom to take control, give it away, and feel the dynamic change.",
            "type_3_customer_tags": "quiz-type-3",
            "type_4_name": "The Director",
            "type_4_tagline": "You don’t want to wait for the right moment. You want to decide exactly how it unfolds.",
            "type_4_percent": 11,
            "type_4_dim1_label": "Adventure",
            "type_4_dim1_value": 94,
            "type_4_dim2_label": "Intensity",
            "type_4_dim2_value": 80,
            "type_4_dim3_label": "Adventure",
            "type_4_dim3_value": 56,
            "type_4_locked_text": "You naturally notice pacing, reactions, and exactly when the energy should build, pause, or change. Expressing what you want doesn’t pull you out of the experience—it draws you deeper into it and makes every response feel more meaningful.\n\nWhat excites you isn’t control alone, but seeing someone respond to your choices and knowing your direction is shaping the experience. Bottom line: you’re most turned on when your intention becomes someone else’s reaction.",
            "type_4_customer_tags": "quiz-type-4",
